# Git remotes — frontend vs backend

This working tree (`D:\lunar final`) has two GitHub remotes. Use them correctly on every commit/push.

| Role | Remote name | GitHub repo |
|------|-------------|-------------|
| **Frontend** (UI / SPA / portals) | `origin` | [Multi-Tenant-Webapp-orvexacloud/D2C-Multi-tenant-webapp](https://github.com/Multi-Tenant-Webapp-orvexacloud/D2C-Multi-tenant-webapp) |
| **Backend** (API / Render) | `orvexacloud` | [GowreeshKP/orvexacloud](https://github.com/GowreeshKP/orvexacloud) |

## What counts as frontend vs backend

- **Frontend**: `src/`, `public/`, `index.html`, Vite/UI config, portal CSS, dashboard/admin/storefront React code
- **Backend**: `server/`, API routes, models, services, `render.yaml`, Express/platform payment code

## Commit and push rules

1. When the user asks to commit and push:
   - **Frontend-only** changes → `git push origin HEAD` (Multi-Tenant-Webapp)
   - **Backend-only** changes → `git push orvexacloud HEAD`
   - **Mixed** frontend + backend in one commit → push **both** `origin` and `orvexacloud`
2. Prefer splitting into separate commits when frontend and backend changes are unrelated, then push each to the matching remote.
3. Never assume a single remote is enough for production: Render deploys from **orvexacloud**; the Multi-Tenant-Webapp repo is the frontend org copy.
4. Marketing site is a **separate** repo under `marketing-site-orvexatechcloud/` (`Multi-Tenant-Webapp-orvexacloud/marketing-site-orvexacloud-`). Commit/push that repo on its own `origin`, not via these remotes.

## Reminder

- Frontend org: **Multi-Tenant-Webapp-orvexacloud**
- Backend repo: **orvexacloud**
